<title>FRANCE: Jordan seeks 100,000 tonnes Oct/Nov wheat.</title>
<headline>Jordan seeks 100,000 tonnes Oct/Nov wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan is tendering on August 12 for 100,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat, European grain traders confirmed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>One shipment of 50,000 tonnes is for October delivery and the rest for November, they said.</p>
<p>The tender had been expected.</p>
<p>On July 23, Jordan bought 100,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at $171.00 and $172.65 per tonne cost and freight for delivery in August and September.</p>
